'' A literal for a 'byref as const string' parameter of a HEADER-declared procedure bound
'' to a runtime alias gets a real temporary, deleted after the call, as fbc gives it --
'' not the pool descriptor fbc reserves for its own runtime procedures, which leaked one
'' slot per call. See the source for fbc's output.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --dump-ir tests/mir/src/header-rt-alias-literal-temp.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-OUT: verify: ok
'' EXPECT-OUT: 0 statements not lowered
'' EXPECT-OUT: fb_StrIsNumeric(
'' EXPECT-OUT: fb_StrDelete(
'' EXPECT-NOT: fb_StrAllocTempDescZEx
